:Namespace Search
    ⍝ Choice of the move to play.

    ⎕IO ⎕ML←1

    ⍝ Score of a side that is checkmated at the root. It exceeds any
    ⍝ material score, so no material balance outweighs a mate.
    MATE←100000

    ⍝ Bound of the default search window. Every score lies strictly
    ⍝ between -INFINITY and INFINITY.
    INFINITY←MATE+1

    ⍝ No search reaches this many half-moves from the root, so a score
    ⍝ within MAX_PLY of ±MATE is a mate.
    MAX_PLY←1000

    negamax←{
        ⍝ Score of a position by negamax search to a fixed depth.
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ lookup tables
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ depth, bitboards, game state[, ply]; ply defaults to 0
        ⍝ ← ←→ score, nodes
        ⍝      score: centipawns from the side to move's point of view;
        ⍝      a side checkmated ply half-moves from the root scores
        ⍝      ply-MATE, so faster mates score higher for the winner
        ⍝      nodes: positions searched, this one included

        lookups←⍺
        (depth bitboards game_state ply)←4↑⍵,0

        side←game_state[##.GameState.side]
        in_check←lookups ##.MoveGeneration.isKingInCheck bitboards side

         ⍝ Check extension: the search continues past the horizon while in
        ⍝ check, so a mate there is still found.
        (depth≤0)∧~in_check:(##.Evaluation.evaluate bitboards game_state)1

        moves←lookups ##.MoveGeneration.generateLegalMoves bitboards game_state
        side←game_state[##.GameState.side]
        ⍝ If there are no legal moves, it is either stalemate (evaluation 0)
        ⍝ or checkmate (evaluation ply-MATE).
        0=≢moves:(in_check×ply-MATE)1

        ⍝ One row of score and nodes per move. Each child's score is from
        ⍝ the opponent's point of view, so it is negated before taking the
        ⍝ maximum.
        children←lookups{⍺ negamax(depth-1),(bitboards game_state ##.MoveGeneration.makeMove ⍵),ply+1}⍤1⊢moves
        (⌈/-⊣/children),1++/⊢/children
    }



    alphaBeta←{
        ⍝ Score of a position by negamax search with alpha-beta pruning.
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ lookup tables
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ depth, bitboards, game state[, alpha, beta[, ply]];
        ⍝      the window defaults to every possible score, ply to 0
        ⍝ ← ←→ score, nodes
        ⍝      score: as negamax when it lies strictly inside the window;
        ⍝      at most alpha when the true score is at most alpha, and at
        ⍝      least beta when the true score is at least beta
        ⍝      nodes: positions searched, this one included

        lookups←⍺
        (depth bitboards game_state alpha beta ply)←⍵,(3-⍨≢⍵)↓(-INFINITY)INFINITY 0

        side←game_state[##.GameState.side]
        in_check←lookups ##.MoveGeneration.isKingInCheck bitboards side

        ⍝ Check extension, as in negamax.
        (depth≤0)∧~in_check:(##.Evaluation.evaluate bitboards game_state)1

        moves←lookups ##.MoveGeneration.generateLegalMoves bitboards game_state
        0=≢moves:(in_check×ply-MATE)1

        (score nodes)←2↑lookups searchMoves depth bitboards game_state alpha beta ply moves
        score(1+nodes)
    }

    searchMoves←{
        ⍝ Alpha-beta search of the positions after each move, in order.
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ lookup tables
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ depth, bitboards, game state, alpha, beta, ply, moves
        ⍝      [, best, best index, nodes, next index];
        ⍝      ply is that of the position the moves are made in, and
        ⍝      moves has at least one row; the trailing items carry the
        ⍝      search so far between moves and are omitted by callers
        ⍝ ← ←→ score, nodes, index
        ⍝      score: best score from the side to move's point of view,
        ⍝      bounded by the window as for alphaBeta
        ⍝      nodes: positions searched, the position itself excluded
        ⍝      index: row of the first move reaching that score

        lookups←⍺
        (depth bitboards game_state alpha beta ply moves best best_index nodes i)←⍵,(¯7+≢⍵)↓(-INFINITY)1 0 1
        i>≢moves:best nodes best_index

        child←bitboards game_state ##.MoveGeneration.makeMove moves[i;]
        (child_score child_nodes)←lookups alphaBeta(depth-1),child,(-beta),(-alpha),ply+1
        improved←best<-child_score
        best←best⌈-child_score
        best_index←(1+improved)⊃best_index i
        nodes←nodes+child_nodes

        ⍝ The search stops once a move reaches beta: the opponent avoids
        ⍝ this position, so the remaining moves cannot change the result.
        best≥beta:best nodes best_index
        lookups ∇ depth bitboards game_state(alpha⌈best)beta ply moves best best_index nodes(i+1)
    }

    bestMove←{
        ⍝ Move with the highest alpha-beta score.
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ lookup tables
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ depth, bitboards, game state
        ⍝ ← ←→ move, score, nodes
        ⍝      move: (from to promotion); ⍬ when there is no legal move
        ⍝      score, nodes: as returned by alphaBeta for the position

        lookups←⍺
        (depth bitboards game_state)←⍵

        moves←lookups ##.MoveGeneration.generateLegalMoves bitboards game_state
        0=≢moves:(⊂⍬),lookups alphaBeta depth bitboards game_state

        ⍝ The first of several equally good moves is chosen, so shuffling
        ⍝ picks one of them at random and keeps variety.
        moves←moves[?⍨≢moves;]
        (score nodes index)←lookups searchMoves depth bitboards game_state(-INFINITY)INFINITY 0 moves
        moves[index;]score(1+nodes)
    }

    randomMove←{
        ⍝ Uniformly random legal move.
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ lookup tables
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ bitboards, game state
        ⍝ ← ←→ move (from to promotion); ⍬ when there is no legal move

        moves←⍺ ##.MoveGeneration.generateLegalMoves ⍵
        0=≢moves:⍬
        moves[?≢moves;]
    }
:EndNamespace